@startuml runtime-02-signing-write
' Runtime scenario 2 - a signing write and the --exec gate.
' Canonical source for docs/architecture/arc42.md section 6.2.
' Shape shared by all four signing commands: wallet send, wallet set-nonce,
' contract transfer-ownership, contract proxy-upgrade.
' The static-call step shown here is the contract pair; wallet send substitutes
' a balance and fee read under --all.

title Runtime scenario 2 - signing write with the --exec gate (evm contract proxy-upgrade)

actor Operator
participant "handler" as H
participant "lib/wallet" as W
participant "lib/chains" as Ch
participant "lib/rpc" as Rpc
participant "JSON-RPC endpoint" as Node

Operator -> H: evm contract proxy-upgrade PROXY NEW_IMPL\n-c base --private-key DEPLOYER_PK [--exec]
activate H

group Local validation - no network, no key needed
  H -> H: addresses well formed, exactly one chain,\namounts parseable, option combination legal
  alt invalid
    H -> Operator: red line on stderr, exit 1
  end
end

H -> W: resolvePrivateKey(flagValue)
activate W
note right of W
  64 hex characters is the key itself.
  Anything else is the name of an
  environment variable holding one.
  The resolved value is never logged.
end note
W --> H: private key, in memory only
deactivate W

H -> Ch: loadProfile, resolveChain
activate Ch
Ch --> H: ResolvedChain
deactivate Ch
H -> Rpc: createProvider(endpoint, chainId)
activate Rpc
Rpc --> H: provider, chain id pinned
deactivate Rpc

group On-chain preconditions
  H -> Node: eth_getCode(proxy), eth_getStorageAt(admin slot),\nProxyAdmin.owner()
  activate Node
  Node --> H: code, admin, admin owner
  deactivate Node
  alt structural: no code at the proxy, empty admin slot, or an EOA admin
    H -> Operator: error in both modes, exit 1
    note left of H
      The address is not the kind of proxy
      this command upgrades, so there is
      nothing to plan either.
    end note
  end
end

H -> Node: eth_call - static-call the upgrade transaction
activate Node
Node --> H: success, or a revert reason
deactivate Node

alt --exec not given (default)
  H -> Operator: prints the plan, the warnings, and the static-call result
  H -> Operator: exit 0
  note left of H
    Exit 0 even when the static call reverted.
    The dry run reports; it does not gate.
  end note
else --exec given
  alt static call reverted
    H -> Operator: "static call reverted, not sending", exit 1
  else implementation has no code
    H -> Operator: refused, exit 1
  else
    note right of H
      "Signer is not the admin owner" stays a
      warning under --exec: the static call
      catches it if it matters, and the
      operator may be simulating for someone else.
    end note
    H -> Node: eth_sendRawTransaction - signed locally by ethers
    activate Node
    Node --> H: transaction hash
    H -> Node: await receipt
    Node --> H: receipt
    deactivate Node
    H -> Node: re-read the implementation slot
    activate Node
    Node --> H: on-chain value after the upgrade
    deactivate Node
    H -> Operator: reports the value actually on chain, exit 0
  end
end

H -> H: provider.destroy() in finally
deactivate H

@enduml
